  "interpretation": "Two seed-0 runs: H2/L1/M1 and H4/L2/M3 at fixed high_alpha=3.0 and low_alpha=3. Training and inference retain predicted mean commands. Stop gradients only where the executor receives the predicted command; high loss retains the original planner output and full recurrent BPTT. High, low and value losses update the shared goal encoder through their remaining paths: the low loss reaches the directly supplied final-goal representation, but its path through predicted planner commands is detached. Shared observation features still receive low-loss gradients. All other architecture, waypoint-final high loss, cumulative-from-current-state weighting, subgoal sampling interval (50), optimizer, data, evaluation and checkpoint settings match the beta-3 v1 runs. No beta schedule, adjacent-difference weights, intermediate supervision or horizon changes. Use physical GPU 1 with two concurrent training processes in a separate frozen campaign.",
